INT. FISHING BOAT, MOORED AT DOCK - DAY

A deposition held in a wheelhouse. A stenographer's machine on a tackle crate. Gulls outside. The boat creaks.

ATTORNEY RENATA OKAFOR-LINDGREN, forties, sharp suit, sea-legs unsteady, leans against a bulkhead. Opposite, in a folding chair, sits CAPTAIN GWENDOLYN "GWEN" HARTIGAN, sixty, weathered, arms crossed.

RENATA
State your name for the record.

GWEN
Gwendolyn Hartigan.

RENATA
And you were the captain on the night of the sixth.

GWEN
I'm captain every night.

Renata slides a photograph across the crate. Gwen doesn't look at it.

RENATA
She was found in your hold.

GWEN
She was my deckhand.

RENATA
And she was alive when she boarded?

GWEN
She was alive when she came on. She was alive when she went below.

Renata taps the photo. Gwen's jaw tightens.

RENATA
And when she came up?

GWEN
She didn't.
